From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 06:30:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: Say when a Teams call was answered on another device

With the attach while ringing, a call answered on another device stops
ringing here, but the call controller's call/end for it (reason
clientError, code 487, "Call cancelled as it was accepted by another
fork.") was mapped to cause "error", and the Phone app showed a missed
call.

Send cause "answeredElsewhere" for that end while the call rings here,
which the Phone app counts as answered. The phrase decides, not 487
alone, which is SIP's "request terminated" and may come for a caller
giving up as well. The member names of every callEnd are now logged
(never values), to see whether a sturdier field than the phrase exists.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 teams_calling.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/teams_calling.c b/teams_calling.c
index 0cf1cc7..04be09b 100644
--- a/teams_calling.c
+++ b/teams_calling.c
@@ -2177,7 +2177,15 @@ teams_calling_handle_trouter(TeamsAccount *sa, JsonObject *body_obj, const gchar
 			 * causes: "normal"/"rejected"/"missed"/"busy"/"error". A normal hang-up (either side) or a
 			 * successfully-connected call that ended = "normal"; declines/timeouts map accordingly. */
 			const gchar *cause = "normal";
-			if (phrase && (strstr(phrase, "Decline") || strstr(phrase, "Reject")))      cause = "rejected";
+			log_member_names("call ended: callEnd", ce);
+			/* Taken on another of the user's devices while it rang here. CAPTURED (sargo, 5 Nov
+			 * 2026, answered on teams.live.com): reason clientError, code 487, phrase "Call
+			 * cancelled as it was accepted by another fork." 487 alone is SIP's "request
+			 * terminated", which a caller giving up may get too, so the phrase decides.
+			 * "answeredElsewhere" makes the Phone app count the call as answered, not missed. */
+			if (cur->state == TEAMS_CALL_INCOMING && phrase && strstr(phrase, "accepted by another fork"))
+				cause = "answeredElsewhere";
+			else if (phrase && (strstr(phrase, "Decline") || strstr(phrase, "Reject")))      cause = "rejected";
 			else if (phrase && (strstr(phrase, "Unanswer") || strstr(phrase, "Timeout") ||
 			                    strstr(phrase, "NoAnswer") || strstr(phrase, "Ring")))   cause = "missed";
 			else if (phrase && strstr(phrase, "Busy"))                                   cause = "busy";
